# Copy to .env next to compose.yaml on both boxes, the same file on each. PEERS is required unless MENTAT=1: edit and
# uncomment it below. Unset, the other settings take the image's defaults (Dockerfile) and TUNE's (knobs.sh).

# --- the two boxes ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Edit these three lines for your boxes, then remove the # from each. They are commented out on purpose: a copy of this
# file never starts the boxes with example addresses (with PEERS unset, the boot stops and says so). With MENTAT=1
# (README.md, "Clustering") leave all three commented out.
# Their 10G LAN addresses, head first. The head serves the API.
#PEERS=<head-lan-ip>,<box2-lan-ip>
# Each box's ConnectX address on PCIe root 1 (IPS) and PCIe root 2 (IPS2), in PEERS order.
#IPS=<head-root1-ip>,<box2-root1-ip>
#IPS2=<head-root2-ip>,<box2-root2-ip>

# --- the knobs (README.md, "Knobs") ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What to prioritize (README.md, "Pick what to prioritize"): speed (the default), context or quality. Each sets
# VARIANT, SESS, CAP and MAX_MODEL_LEN, and context also turns on context-parallel KV (knobs.sh). A value set below
# keeps its value.
#TUNE=speed
# The width manifest of the release: bit349 for speed and context, k4 for quality.
#VARIANT=bit349
# The requests that decode at once: 8 for speed and context, 4 for quality.
#SESS=8
# The KV pool in tokens, shared by the sessions, a multiple of 64: 2097152 for speed and context, 262208 for quality.
#CAP=2097152
# The longest single request, prompt and output together, at most CAP less the guard rows (and 1,048,576):
# 262144 for speed and quality, 1048576 for context.
#MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144
# 1: a request alone drafts with the DFlash2 drafter, fetched from Hugging Face and converted on the first
# boot (its licence is CC BY-NC-ND 4.0). 0: MTP only, and the drafter is never fetched.
#DFLASH=1
# 0: the boxes in PEERS. 1: find the other box and register the API through the host's mentat daemon, in group GROUP.
#MENTAT=0
#GROUP=gr8-glm53f-2x
# Image input is on: the recipe adds GR8_GLM53F_VISION=1 to EXTRA_ENV unless EXTRA_ENV already names it. Each box loads
# the vision tower (about 1.6 GiB of memory). To turn it off, put GR8_GLM53F_VISION=0 in EXTRA_ENV, with anything else
# EXTRA_ENV holds, on both boxes:
#EXTRA_ENV="GR8_GLM53F_VISION=0"
# Reply and thinking length (gr8 frontend/README.md, soft thinking budget). A request with no max_tokens gets 32,768.
# From the 16,384th thinking token the </think> logit gains 4 a thousand tokens, up to 10; empty turns it off. The hard
# budget closes the thinking at 28,672 tokens; 0 = no limit. A request's own max_tokens, think_end_boost or
# thinking_budget wins.
#DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS=32768
#DEFAULT_THINK_END_BOOST="start=16384,per1k=4,max=10"
#DEFAULT_THINKING_BUDGET=28672

# --- host directories in place of the named volumes, each owned by uid 1000 ------------------------------------------
#MODEL_CACHE_DIR=/srv/glm53f/cache      # this box's part of the model and of the drafter (README.md, What you need)
#PROMPT_CACHE_DIR=/srv/glm53f/prompts   # the prompt cache, up to 64 GB (kv-store.yaml)
#GR8_HOME_DIR=/srv/glm53f/home          # logs and state

# --- compact expert copies (README.md, "Compact expert copies") -----------------------------------------------------
# Off by default. To turn on, on both boxes: remove the `#` from the EXTRA_ENV line below, write the copies once with
# `docker compose run --rm gr8 prepare`, and restart. The loader then reads dense per-rank copies of its expert
# ranges. A switch from GLM-5.3 into this recipe took 26.9 / 25.2 s with both settings, against 33.5 / 33.5 s without
# (two DGX Sparks, TP=2, n=2 each). The copies take 73 GiB a box in the cache volume, beside the release. These
# numbers were measured with VARIANT=k4 on release pin 867580abd28d142bb4c56218bb81a752b7dea988
# (kindlingai/glm-5.3-flash-exlr8-k2-k3-k4), the pin before this recipe's bit349 default (PR #14, 8f1992b; the current
# pin is 901ad084f0afd2400820504910d3e684133ce183). bit349 (the default, TUNE=speed) was not measured. If the line is
# on and `prepare` has not run, the loader finds no copies and reads the release as before, except GR8_LOAD_MERGE_KB=1
# still merges nearby reads (ranges at most 1 KB apart, gaps included); there is no number for that. A different
# VARIANT (TUNE=quality uses k4), TP size or release needs its own directory and its own prepare. Both boxes need the
# same line.
# To turn it off again, comment the line out. The copies stay in the volume until you delete the directory.
#EXTRA_ENV="GR8_LOAD_COMPACT=/var/lib/gr8/cache/compact-tp2 GR8_LOAD_MERGE_KB=1"

# --- the image ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A pinned image in place of latest, e.g. ghcr.io/kindlingai/glm-5.3-flash-exlr8-2x-spark:sha-<commit>
#IMAGE=

# --- other -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The release and the drafter, each pinned to a Hugging Face commit (https://huggingface.co/<org>/<repo>@<commit>).
# The image pins the commits measured in README.md; drop the @<commit> to follow the repo's main.
#MODEL=https://huggingface.co/kindlingai/glm-5.3-flash-exlr8-k2-k3-k4@901ad084f0afd2400820504910d3e684133ce183
#DRAFTER=https://huggingface.co/incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2@bf582e4eacc1810f76656d1811693ff6c6737d2a
# Sent only to Hugging Face, for a gated or private repo
#HF_TOKEN=
# Any other gr8 launcher option (gr8/KNOBS.md) works here too, as NAME=VALUE.
